{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1000", "sample_idx": 24, "model_name": "abacusai/dracarys-llama-3.1-70b-instruct", "content": "Raymond III Count of Tripoli was the Count of Tripoli from 1152 to 1187. He was the son of Raymond II Count of Tripoli and Hodierna of Jerusalem. Raymond III was a member of the House of Toulouse and the ruler of the Crusader state of the County of Tripoli.\n\n*Early Life and Succession*\nRaymond III was born around 1140. He succeeded his father Raymond II as the Count of Tripoli in 1152. Raymond III was still a minor when he ascended to the throne and the county was governed by his mother Hodierna and the constable of the county Humphrey II of Toron.\n\nRaymond III was a vassal of the Kingdom of Jerusalem and participated in several military campaigns against the Muslim forces. In 1153 he joined King Baldwin III of Jerusalem in the siege of Ascalon. In 1157 he fought against Nur ad-Din the ruler of Aleppo and Damascus in the Battle of Jacob's Ford.\n\n*Conflict with the Kingdom of Jerusalem*\nRaymond III had a complicated relationship with the Kingdom of Jerusalem. In 1164 he was taken prisoner by the Muslims and was released after a ransom was paid. He then joined the forces of King Amalric I of Jerusalem in the siege of Alexandria. However in 1170 he refused to provide military support to the kingdom during the invasion of Egypt.\n\n*Later Life and Death*\nRaymond III died in 1187 during the Battle of Hattin. He was succeeded by his godson Raymond IV of Antioch. Raymond III was married to Eschiva of Bures and had no children. He was known for his bravery and military skills but also for his conflicts with the Kingdom of Jerusalem.\n\n*Capture and Imprisonment*\nIn 1164 Raymond III was captured by the Muslims during a battle near the castle of Chastellet. He was taken prisoner and held in Aleppo. He was released after a ransom was paid by the Knights Hospitaller.\n\n*Relationship with the Military Orders*\nRaymond III had a close relationship with the military orders of the Knights Templar and the Knights Hospitaller. He granted them several lands and privileges in the County of Tripoli.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Ray", "logprob": -0.004134069196879864}, {"token": "mond", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " III", "logprob": -6.318112355074845e-06}, {"token": " Count", "logprob": -0.35264554619789124}, {"token": " of", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " Trip", "logprob": -3.814704541582614e-06}, {"token": "oli", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " was", "logprob": -0.014512372203171253}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.6300244927406311}, {"token": " Count", "logprob": -0.20569056272506714}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -2.3841860752327193e-07}, {"token": " Trip", "logprob": -9.536747711536009e-07}, {"token": "oli", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " from", "logprob": -0.0004266814503353089}, {"token": " ", "logprob": -0.0007029857952147722}, {"token": "115", "logprob": -2.1696325347875245e-05}, {"token": "2", "logprob": -8.833798347041011e-05}, {"token": " to", "logprob": -0.11100077629089355}, {"token": " ", "logprob": -0.006717844400554895}, {"token": "118", "logprob": -8.941096166381612e-05}, {"token": "7", "logprob": -6.997830496402457e-05}, {"token": ".", "logprob": -0.2691226601600647}, {"token": " He", "logprob": -0.006646439433097839}, {"token": " was", "logprob": -0.002608718816190958}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.09799444675445557}, {"token": " son", "logprob": -0.021196268498897552}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -1.0967314665322192e-05}, {"token": " Raymond", "logprob": -0.0009513252880424261}, {"token": " II", "logprob": -7.391003236989491e-06}, {"token": " Count", "logprob": -0.14850078523159027}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -3.695494797284482e-06}, {"token": " Trip", "logprob": -1.1920935776288388e-06}, {"token": "oli", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " and", "logprob": -9.680262883193791e-05}, {"token": " H", "logprob": -0.01590247079730034}, {"token": "odi", "logprob": -3.57628505298635e-06}, {"token": "erna", 